# Beamwidth source audit (Task 1 only)

`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM` — no constant or sealed/engine path was changed.

## Finding

**HOBS uses `theta_3dB = 0.058 rad` as the one-sided angle from boresight to
the half-power point.** It is not the full angular span between the two
half-power points. The source-implied full HPBW is therefore `0.116 rad =
6.6463104235 deg`.

Completion criterion: verify the cited paper's equation and Table I row in a
retrievable primary-source copy, resolve the angle convention from the equation,
and trace convention-coupled constants and downstream geometry in the engine.
This criterion is met.

## Primary source and custody

Sz-Han Chen, Li-Hsiang Shen, Kai-Ten Feng, Lie-Liang Yang, and Jen-Ming Wu,
“Energy-Efficient Joint Handover and Beam Switching Scheme for Multi-LEO
Networks,” *2024 IEEE 99th Vehicular Technology Conference
(VTC2024-Spring)*, DOI
[10.1109/VTC2024-Spring62846.2024.10683088](https://doi.org/10.1109/VTC2024-Spring62846.2024.10683088).

- [Official VTC conference PDF](https://ieeevtc.org/vtc2024spring/DATA/PID2024002205.pdf)
- [IEEE Xplore record](https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10683088)
- Audited local IEEE PDF:
  [reference PDF](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/.scratch/chinese-word-r1-symbols-20260905-r1/input/thesis-mc/references-pdf/%5B04%5D_Energy_Efficient_Joint_Handover_and_Beam_Switching_S.pdf),
  7 pages, SHA-256
  `1b2a8eda4647c4f7b68f8ffb08347aaa9cde18ae32b7d6af84d68f827a0f3089`.
  This digest matches the repository's prior custody record in
  [`ADR-002`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/docs/decisions/ADR-002-proposed-hobs-primary-geometry.md:20).

## Verbatim source evidence

Equation (3), PDF page 2:

> \(G(\theta)=G_0\left[\frac{J_1(\mu(\theta))}{2\mu(\theta)}+36\frac{J_3(\mu(\theta))}{\mu(\theta)^3}\right]^2.\tag{3}\)

The same paragraph defines:

> \(\mu(\theta)=2.07123\cdot\sin(\theta)/\sin(\theta_{3dB})\)

Its short prose definitions are “where theta is the boresight angle” and
“theta_3dB is the 3 dB half-power beamwidth angle of the antenna.”

Table I, PDF page 6, verbatim row:

> `3dB beamwidth θ₃dB    0.058 rad`

The math has been transcribed typographically without changing the source's
operators, subscripts, coefficient, or value.

## Why the equation settles the convention

At `theta = theta_3dB`, the source's denominator cancels its numerator and
`mu = 2.07123`. Direct high-precision evaluation of equation (3) gives

```text
G(theta_3dB) / G_0 = 0.5000004083327867
10 log10(G/G_0)     = -3.0102964099 dB
```

At `theta = 0`, the Bessel-expression limit is one, so `G(0) = G_0`; the
pattern is symmetric about boresight. Thus the parameter used as the angular
argument in the equation is the radial/off-boresight location of the
half-power boundary. The full width of a one-dimensional cut is the span from
`-theta_3dB` to `+theta_3dB`, namely twice the table value:

```text
source half-power off-axis angle = 0.058 rad = 3.3231552118 deg
source-implied full HPBW          = 0.116 rad = 6.6463104235 deg
```

HOBS does not itself print `0.116 rad`; that full-span value is the necessary
consequence of its equation. The table heading alone is linguistically
ambiguous, but the equation is not: it contains `sin(theta_3dB)`, not
`sin(theta_3dB/2)`.

## Engine reading and propagation audit

| Item | What the code/source does | Convention impact |
|---|---|---|
| `TX_FULL_HPBW_DEG = 3.32` | Declared as a full HPBW in [`constants_v025.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/constants_v025.py:76). [`channel.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/channel.py:99) divides it by two before putting it in the denominator of `mu`. | The V0.25 pattern's half-power edge is `1.66 deg`, half the HOBS off-axis value. At the engine's `theta = 3.32 deg`, its normalized gain is only `0.0423687169` (`-13.72955 dB`), not one half. |
| `_BESSEL_MU_COEFFICIENT = 2.07123` | Copied from HOBS equation (3) in [`channel.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/channel.py:39). | Correct and invariant; the convention error is the extra halving of the angle supplied to its denominator. |
| `TX_G0_LINEAR = 2000` | Not HOBS Table I's `40 dBi` (`10000`). The legacy antenna record says it was re-derived from `D = 1.0275 lambda / theta_3dB` using the narrower full-width convention and an external aperture-efficiency range; see [`env/antenna.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/env/antenna.py:46). | This is convention-coupled provenance. Under that same project aperture/width relation, doubling full HPBW halves `D/lambda` and quarters gain, giving about `500`; the repository correctly labels that as an unresolved conditional candidate, not a HOBS value ([`ADR-002`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/docs/decisions/ADR-002-proposed-hobs-primary-geometry.md:140)). A width-only diagnostic that holds `2000` fixed is therefore a deliberate sensitivity, not a fully re-derived HOBS geometry. |
| Legacy `env.THETA_3DB_DEG = 3.32` | Duplicates the full-span reading in both [`env/antenna.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/env/antenna.py:43) and [`env/cells.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/env/cells.py:49). `cell_radius_km` also halves it. | The same interpretation propagates beyond link gain into cell radius, lattice pitch, coverage, and any frozen pointing-cell selection built from that grid. [`prereg.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/runtime/prereg.py:626) records that geometry explicitly. |
| `REFERENCE_BEAMS_PER_SATELLITE = 39` and derived `REFERENCE_AGGREGATE_RF_W` | V0.25 calls `39` a compatibility reference rather than a hardware ceiling in [`constants_v025.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/constants_v025.py:88). HOBS Table I says `37`, so `39` is not copied from HOBS. | Not an arithmetic dependent of `TX_FULL_HPBW_DEG` in V0.25, but its project lineage is the narrow-grid coverage selection, so a geometry rebuild must not assume its provenance survives a width change. |
| `HOBS_REFERENCE_MAX_RF_W = 100` | Literal conversion of HOBS Table I's `P_max = 50 dBm`, retained only as a non-live compatibility reference in [`constants_v025.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/constants_v025.py:90). | Same paper, but independent of the angle convention; no propagation. |

No other constant in `src/mcrl/physics_v025` arithmetically depends on
`TX_FULL_HPBW_DEG`. The actual V0.25 dependence is confined to the transmit
pattern calculation; the separate legacy `env` geometry carries the broader
cell/lattice dependence described above.

One additional provenance caution: [`env/antenna.py`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-beam-ws/src/mcrl/env/antenna.py:65)
says the paper fixes an on-axis cutoff of `1e-10`. A full-text search of the
audited HOBS PDF finds no `1e-10` cutoff; HOBS states the analytic pattern but
does not state that numerical implementation tolerance. This does not affect
the beamwidth conclusion, but it should not be attributed to HOBS without a
different cited source.

## Task-bound conclusion

The reported audit reading is correct: HOBS's `0.058 rad` is the half-power
off-axis angle, implying a full span twice as wide as the engine's registered
`3.32 deg` full HPBW. This is a source-definition finding only. It neither
changes a constant nor recommends selecting a width from outcome performance.
